      <para>Use these initial Keplerian states in EarthMJ2000Eq, all at
      UTCGregorian epoch 01 Jan 2000 11:59:27.966. SMA is in km and angles are
      in degrees. Sat1's screenshot has a numerical eccentricity near
      1.36e-16; the replacement uses the equivalent circular value zero.
      Sat2 and Sat3 use eccentricity 0.0005 and opposite small inclination,
      node and phase offsets. Sat4 uses a small inclination and phase offset.
      These choices keep a nearby formation on the same nominal semimajor
      axis while providing a nontrivial transfer for Sat2.</para>

