  <section>
    <title>Running the Mission</title>

    <para>Save the mission, then run it. The twenty Report commands write
    FormationRendezvousTutorial.data. With the report’s default solver-iteration
    setting, the target branches also write repeated Sat1–Sat4 groups for
    nominal and perturbed solver passes. In the Window menu, select the solver
    progress window for Target1 and verify Converged and a residual below
    0.0001 km for each position component. Select Target2’s progress window
    and verify each inertial velocity difference is below 0.0001 km/s.
    DifferentialCorrectorDC.data records the last target’s achieved values,
    and Mission → Mission summary lets you inspect and save command endpoint
    states. The final 0.2-day coast follows Target2 and adds no constraints.</para>

    <para>The downloadable reconstructed script adds a separate
    FormationRendezvousResiduals.data diagnostic report and suppresses trial
    rows in its Cartesian report. Those additional diagnostic variables and
    assignments are not created by the steps above. Both missions demonstrate
    the same two separate targeting goals. Position remains unconstrained at
    the later velocity-match endpoint.</para>

